{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4747310","formula":"H₈N₂MoS₄","hill":"H8MoN2S4","elements":["H","N","S","Mo"],"composition":{"H":8.0,"N":2.0,"S":4.0,"Mo":1.0},"names":{"en":"Ammonium tetrathiomolybdate","ru":"Тетратиомолибдат аммония"},"descriptions":{"en":"Ammonium tetrathiomolybdate is the chemical compound with the formula (NH4)2MoS4. This bright red ammonium salt is an important reagent in the chemistry of molybdenum and has been used as a building block in bioinorganic chemistry. The thiometallate (see metallate) anion has the distinctive property of undergoing oxidation at the sulfur centers concomitant with reduction of the metal from Mo(VI) to Mo(IV).","ru":"Тетратиомолибдат аммония — химическое соединение с формулой (NH4)2MoS4. Ярко-красная соль аммония является важным реагентом в химических реакциях молибдена и используется в качестве основы в биоорганической химии. Растворяется в воде, этаноле и гидроокиси аммония."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":15251598,"mass":262.3,"charge":0,"smiles":"[NH4+].[NH4+].[SH-].[SH-].S=[Mo]=S","inchikey":"ZKKLPDLKUGTPME-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"diazanium;bis(sulfanylidene)molybdenum;sulfanide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1199487","atoms":66,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[9.653,0.0,0.0],[0.0,7.085,0.0],[0.0,0.0,12.17]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":7.272,"y":5.314,"z":0.844,"el":"Mo"},{"x":2.446,"y":5.314,"z":5.241,"el":"Mo"},{"x":2.381,"y":1.771,"z":11.326,"el":"Mo"},{"x":7.207,"y":1.771,"z":6.929,"el":"Mo"},{"x":2.581,"y":5.314,"z":1.654,"el":"H"},{"x":7.407,"y":5.314,"z":4.431,"el":"H"},{"x":7.072,"y":1.771,"z":10.516,"el":"H"},{"x":2.246,"y":1.771,"z":7.739,"el":"H"},{"x":0.967,"y":5.314,"z":2.125,"el":"H"},{"x":5.793,"y":5.314,"z":3.96,"el":"H"},{"x":8.686,"y":1.771,"z":10.045,"el":"H"},{"x":3.859,"y":1.771,"z":8.21,"e